 **Status:** proposed; counts as accepted once the orchestrator has verified v0.4.7 (§0 item 20 (3)). Nothing in this document is decided except the owner decisions quoted in §0; every choice is listed under "Decisions" with its alternatives and the null option. Decider for every choice: the owner (human).
 **Scope:** CDP6 is a framework of skills, agents, hooks and deterministic checkers for Claude Code that carries one `intake` (an idea, a feature request, an issue or a bug report, all treated alike) through the full engineering cycle (idea, exploration, concept, refinement, implementation, tests and verification, retro, loop back to exploration) in three modes of equal standing: one session (single-agent mode), an orchestrating main session with spoke subagents (multi-agent mode), and a team lead with conversing teammates (team mode); each mode enforces the same contract, counters, captures and phase gates (ledger 0021 acceptance G1b), and the cycle can run unattended up to a human-set autonomy level. It lives in its own plugin area (`plugins/cdp6-core`) with its own agent and skill namespace, hooks, data directory and doctrine document. **Not included:** changes to the CDP5 plugins (`cdp5-agents`, `cdp5-gates`, `domain-agents`, `orbit-workflow` stay as they are until their removal; the `cdp5-gates` and `domain-agents` parts worth keeping are rebuilt for CDP6 by the carry-over of §11.5, §0 item 24); new domain packs; hosts other than Claude Code; publication steps (push, merge, release, external messages), which stay with the human at every autonomy level; the code itself (this step names the files to be built and builds none).
 
